<title>GERMANY: Siemens workers seek blocking of unit sale.</title>
<headline>Siemens workers seek blocking of unit sale.</headline>
<dateline>MUNICH, Germany 1997-05-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Employees of German industrial group Siemens AG on Wednesday asked the German defence minister to prevent the sale of Siemens' defence electronics business.</p>
<p>The works councils of defence unit appealed to Defence Minister Volker Ruehe to push Siemens to keep at least a minority position in the business. The workers, who feared a new owner would cut jobs, also wanted to prevent a splitting up of the German operations of the defence unit.</p>
<p>Siemens said in February it planned to sell the unit, which included Siemens-Plessey in Britain, to a company with core focus on the defence business.</p>
<p>-- Bonn Newsroom, +49-228 26097150</p>
